          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Reaganomics</strong><br>\nAs president, Reagan implemented his economic policies, known as \"Reaganomics,\" aimed at reducing tax rates, controlling the money supply to reduce inflation, and cutting government spending. Though controversial, these policies were credited with creating a period of economic growth in the United States during the 1980s.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Cold War</strong><br>\nReagan took a firm stand against the Soviet Union, famously demanding \"Mr. Gorbachev, tear down this wall!\" in a speech at the Berlin Wall. His administration saw a significant build-up of U.S. military forces and the beginning of the end of the Cold War, which concluded shortly after his presidency.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy and Death</strong><br>\nAfter leaving office in 1989, Reagan's legacy continued to influence U.S. politics, with many considering him a transformative figure who reshaped national policy and the Republican Party. He passed away on June 5, 2004, after a long battle with Alzheimer's disease, but remains a significant icon in American history.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
